          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em homotopy fiber sequence
            is a “long left-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"}> exact sequence
            ” in an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            = succeed ".)" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofiber+sequence"} cofiber sequence
          %p
            Traditionally, fiber sequences were considered in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+category"} homotopical categories
            such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model categories
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} Brown categories of fibrant objects
            which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} present
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            in question. In particular, this was considered for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            itself. In these cases, they are obtained in terms of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullbacks"} homotopy pullbacks
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            of any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
            of this morphism, one often also speaks of
            = succeed "." do
              %em fibration sequences
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %h3#in_category_theory
            In
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            with small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            and consider
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+objects"} pointed objects
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {*} \to A
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {*}
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            Notice that in the case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            happens to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} stable (∞,1)-category
            for which
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {*} = 0
          %p
            But for the notion of fibration sequence to make sense, we do not need to assume that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a stable
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            (see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gerbe"} gerbe
            and
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            = succeed "-categories." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          %p
            Now let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to B
            be a morphism in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            The
            %strong homotopy fiber
            or
            %strong homotopy kernel
            or
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+cocone"} mapping cocone
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            (which, in our
            = succeed "-categorical" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy pullback
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
