          %h3#in_categories_of_fibrant_objects In categories of fibrant objects
          %blockquote
            %p under construction
          %p
            In (
            %a{:href => "#Quillen67"}> Quillen 67, section I.3
            ), it was shown how the theory of fiber sequences and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofiber+sequences"} cofiber sequences
            arises in the abstract homotopy theory of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+categories"} model categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
            inside the model category, and in fact makes sense generally in this context. This was spelled out in (
            %a{:href => "#Brown73"}> Brown 73, section 4
            ), which we review here.
          #FiberOfFibrationIsCompatibleWithWeakEquivalences.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              In
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+objects"} pointed objects
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_f^{\ast/}
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_f
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FullSubcategoriesOfFibrantCofibrantObjects"}
              = succeed "-diagrams," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi fib
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi Fib
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi fib
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi Fib
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi f
                                  %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    fib(f_1) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X_1 &amp;\underoverset{\in Fib}{f_1}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y_1
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    fib(f_2) &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; X_2 &amp;\underoverset{\in Fib}{f_2}{\longrightarrow}&amp; Y_2
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p If the two vertical morphisms on the right are weak equivalences, then so is the vertical morphism in the left
          %p
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BrownAHT"}> Brown 73, section 4, lemma 3
            )
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p Factor the diagram in question
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
