          %h3#LongSequCoh Long exact sequences in cohomology
          %p
            Usually, when looking at fibration sequences in 1-categorical contexts of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category of an (∞,1)-category
          %p This can be usefully understood as follows:
          %p
            recall from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            objects in an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            that is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is just
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_C(X,A)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Ho
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H(X,A) = \Pi_0 Hom_C(X,A) = Ho_C(X,A)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ho
                    %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho_C
            is the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category+of+an+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} homotopy category of an (∞,1)-category
          %p
            The upshot being that in the right
            = succeed "-context" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
          %p
            But the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
            has the crucial property that it is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+functor"} exact functor
            in both arguments. This holds for
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi K
                          %mi B
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  A \times_K B &amp;\to&amp; B
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  A &amp;\to&amp; K
                  }
          %p
            a homotopy pullback in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in K
            the induced diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mi K
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi B
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  Hom_C(X,A \times_K B) &amp;\to&amp; Hom_C(X,B)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  Hom_C(X,A) &amp;\to&amp; Hom_C(X,K)
                  }
          %p
            is again homotopy pullback diagram (of
            = succeed ");" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mi K
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo ×
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Hom
                        %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_C(X,A \times_K B)\to Hom_C(X,A) \times_{Hom_{C}(X,K)} Hom_C(X,B)
            induced by the universal property of homotopy pullback is an equivalence.
          %p So in particular for
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi ker
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
