            %p
              The homotopy fiber of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(X,B) \stackrel{f_*}{\to} Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(X,C)
              over a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c : X \to C
              may be identified with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object+in+a+quasi-category"} hom-object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{\mathcal{C}_{/C}}(c,f)
            %p
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/over+quasi-category"} over (∞,1)-category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}_{/C}
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} HTT, prop. 5.5.5.12
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              Model all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
              as
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-categories"} quasi-categories
            %p
              Using the discussion at
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object+in+a+quasi-category"} hom-object in a quasi-category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(X,C) \simeq \mathcal{C}_{/C} \times_{\mathcal{C}} \{X\}
            %p and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{\mathcal{C}}(X,B) \simeq \mathcal{C}_{/B} \times_{\mathcal{C}} \{X\}
                    \\simeq \mathcal{C}_{/f} \times_{\mathcal{C}} \{X\}
            %p
              under which identification the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*
              is induced by the canonical
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ″
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi C
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi''  : \mathcal{C}_{/f} \to \mathcal{C}_{/C}
                    \\,.
            %p
              So we are done if we can show that the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi f
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi 𝒞
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                    %mi C
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi f
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mo ′
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi C
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/f} \times_{\mathcal{C}_{/C}} \{c\}
                    \&amp;\to&amp; \mathcal{C}_{/f} \times_{\mathcal{C}} \{X\}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\phi}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\phi'}}
                    \\\
                    \\{c\} &amp;\to&amp; \mathcal{C}_{/C} \times_{\mathcal{C}} \{X\}
                    }
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
              square, because we have an isomorphism of simplicial sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi X
                      %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/f} \times_{\mathcal{C}_{/C}} \{c\}
                    \\simeq
                    Hom^R_{\mathcal{C}_{/X}}(c,f)
                    \\,,
            %p as one checks.
            %p
              Since in the above diagram all objects are
              = succeed "es," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi'
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
              for which in turn it is sufficient that it is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+fibration"} left fibration
            %p That follows by noticing that the right vertical morphism fits into the pullback diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi f
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi f
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mo ′
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi ϕ
                                  %mo ″
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi C
                            %msub
                              %mo ×
                              %mi 𝒞
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒞
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                %mi C
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/f} \times_{\mathcal{C}} \{X\} &amp;\to&amp; \mathcal{C}_{/f}
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^{\mathrlap{\phi'}} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{\phi''}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/C} \times_{\mathcal{C}} \{X\}
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    \\mathcal{C}_{/C}
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              But by general properties of
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+fibration"} left fibration
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi'
          %h3#principal_bundles
            Principal
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            Fibration sequences are familiar from the context of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            denote the corresponding one-object
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            (in the world of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}G
          %p Notice that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Ω
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G \simeq \Omega \mathbf{B} G
                  \\,.
          %p
            Then that a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \to X
            is classified by morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbf{B}G
            means that it is the homotopy fiber of this morphism.
          %p
            Indeed, as indicated at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} generalized universal bundle
            and at
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy limit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P &amp;\to&amp; {*}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                  }
          %p
            by first forming the standard
            %em fibrant replacement
            of the diagram
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ←
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbf{B}G \leftarrow {*}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ←
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                  %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \to \mathbf{B}G \leftarrow \mathbf{E}G
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                  %mi G
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E}G \simeq {*}
            is the total “space” (or 2-groupoid) of the universal
            = succeed "-bundle." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+pullback"} homotopy pullback
            may be computed as the
            %em ordinary
            pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi E
                          %mi G
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P &amp;\to &amp; \mathbf{E}G
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\hat X &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p
            in the ordinary 1-category of
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mover
                    %mo ↠
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X \stackrel{\simeq}{\twoheadrightarrow} X
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            by an acyclic fibration (called “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercover"}> hypercover
            ” in this context) (for instance the Čech groupoid associated with an open cover of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            One recognizes the usual statement that principal
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            The fact that such pullbacks really are bundles whose fiber is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is the statement of the long fibration sequence induced by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
            which says that picking any point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo *
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {*} \to X
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and then pulling back
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            to that point (i.e. restricting it to that point) yields
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                    %mi G
